-- New and updated one-liners (Game Info in Civilopedia)
-----------------------------------------------------------
UPDATE Language_en_US SET Text = 'Mythical spring which supposedly restores the youth of anyone who drinks or bathes in its waters. Tales of such a fountain have been recounted around the world for thousands of years. Based on these many legends, explorers and adventurers looked for this elusive place or some other remedy to aging, generally associated with magic waters.' WHERE Tag = 'TXT_KEY_CIV5_FEATURES_FOUNTAIN_YOUTH_HELP';
UPDATE Language_en_US SET Text = 'Mythical city of gold where according to many legends kings were so rich that they would cover themselves from head to foot in gold dust. The legend is inspired by the culture of indigenous people and spread out among the settlers from more advanced civilizations. In the decades that followed, the city was sought for in various places across the continent.' WHERE Tag = 'TXT_KEY_CIV5_FEATURES_EL_DORADO_HELP';
UPDATE Language_en_US SET Text = 'A large dormant volcano, the highest free-standing mountain above sea level in the world composed of three volcanic cones. It is a major hiking and climbing destination, not so technically challenging, but posing a serious risk of altitude sickness. Climbers experience a journey through multiple climate zones, from tropical to an arctic, resulting in very low success rate for reaching the summit.' WHERE Tag = 'TXT_KEY_CIV5_FEATURES_KILIMANJARO_HELP';
UPDATE Language_en_US SET Text = 'A sacred mountain, where according to many legends there is a footprint of a holy person, different one, depending on which of four main religions mentions about it. The mountain is seen as a symbol of unity across different faiths. It is a common pilgrimage destination, unique because of illuminated paths and many rest stops offering assistance to climbers.' WHERE Tag = 'TXT_KEY_CIV5_FEATURES_SRI_PADA_HELP';

INSERT INTO Language_en_US
			(Tag,											Text)
VALUES		('TXT_KEY_CIV5_FEATURES_CRATER_HELP',			'Formed by the impact of a nickel-iron meteorite, it is one of the largest craters in the world. The lack of erosion has preserved the crater''s shape, allowing it to be used for training Apollo astronauts and numerous other space missions. Despite attempts to make the crater a public landmark, it remains privately owned by the Barringer family.'),
			('TXT_KEY_CIV5_FEATURES_FUJI_HELP',				'An active stratovolcano located on the intersection of three tectonic plates, being one of the "Three Sacred Mountains", a place of exceptional scenic beauty, and a historic site. According to UNESCO, it "has inspired artists and poets and been a site of pilgrimage for centuries".'),
			('TXT_KEY_CIV5_FEATURES_MESA_HELP',				'As the world''s largest flat-topped mountain it offers a dramatic contrast in landscape, climate, and vegetation. The plateau surrounds many river valleys, including the Grand Valley to the west. Its vast surface is dotted with hundreds of scattered lakes, including many reservoirs used for drinking water and irrigation.'),
			('TXT_KEY_CIV5_FEATURES_NEW_REEF_HELP',			'World''s largest coral reef system, consisting of hundreds of individual reefs and islands and stretching over thousands of kilometers. It can be seen from space and is the world''s largest single structure made of living organisms. This incredible animal structure supports an extraordinary diversity of life, including many vulnerable or endangered species.'),
			('TXT_KEY_CIV5_FEATURES_VOLCANO_HELP',			'A caldera formed by a series of powerful explosions, the most violent in recorded history, killing thousands of people, and still active. Summer temperatures in the northern hemisphere dropped significantly in the year following the eruption, and even later a new island, Anak Krakatau or "Child of Krakatau", emerged from the caldera.'),
			('TXT_KEY_CIV5_FEATURES_GIBRALTAR_HELP',		'A monolithic limestone mountain marking the entrance to the Mediterranean Sea. It serves as a fortress and contains a labyrinthine network of man-made tunnels, and at the same time its upper section comprises a nature reserve, home to hundreds of barbary macaques. According to ancient Greek legend, it marked (with Monte Hacho) the western boundary of the known world.'),
			('TXT_KEY_CIV5_FEATURES_GEYSER_HELP',			'A cone geyser known of a highly predictable geothermal activity and spectacular effects. It has been errupting every hour to two hours for few decades. It is not the tallest or largest geyser in the park, but its famous among tourists and scientists because of its reliability that can be attributed to the fact that it is not connected to any other thermal features.'),
			('TXT_KEY_CIV5_FEATURES_POTOSI_HELP',			'A mountain popularly conceived of as being "made of" silver ore, and it is famous for providing vast quantities of silver during colonization era. As a result of mining operations in the mountain, the nearby city became one of the largest cities in the New World, finally changing the mountain into a barren wasteland.'),
			('TXT_KEY_CIV5_FEATURES_MT_SINAI_HELP',			'One of several locations claimed to be the biblical Mount Sinai, the place where, according to the sacred scriptures of the three major Abrahamic religions, Prophet Moses received the Ten Commandments from God. It is surrounded on all sides by higher peaks in the mountain range of which it is a part.'),
			('TXT_KEY_CIV5_FEATURES_MT_KAILASH_HELP',		'A mountain located at the trijunction, being a holy peak of four different religions. Because of that, it is a very common pilgrimage destination for people from over the world. While the mountain has been surveyed by climbers in the past, there has been no recorded successful ascent of the mountain, and now climbing is prohibited due to its religious significance.'),
			('TXT_KEY_CIV5_FEATURES_ULURU_HELP',			'A large sandstone monolith, that crops out off the centre of the continent, surrounded by wide plains. The area around the formation is also home to an abundance of springs, waterholes, rock caves and ancient paintings. Such paintings can be found because this large rock is a sacred place to many native tribes and very important indigenous site.'),
			('TXT_KEY_CIV5_FEATURES_LAKE_VICTORIA_HELP',	'The world''s largest tropical lake and the world''s second-largest fresh water lake by surface area. What is more, it plays a huge role in sustaining the longest river on Earth. This lake is home to many kinds of endemic fish, but because of the appearance of some invasive species many of them were driven to extinction.'),
			('TXT_KEY_CIV5_FEATURES_SOLOMONS_MINES_HELP',	'Mythical mines where enormous amonts of gold were accumulated by the King Solomon. He was known as a powerful, wise and incredibly wealthy ruler. For centuries, adventurers unsuccessfully have tried to find the secret of Solomon''s wealth.'),
			('TXT_KEY_CIV5_FEATURES_SALAR_HELP',			'The world''s largest salt flat, formed by the transformation of several prehistoric lakes that evaporated over time. It is a great source of salt and very rich deposit of lithium. Thanks for its flatness it is ideal for calibrating the altimeters of Earth observation satellites, and after rain, it transforms into the world''s largest mirror.'),
			('TXT_KEY_CIV5_FEATURES_CAUSEWAY_HELP',			'An area of thousands of interconnected basalt columns, the result of an ancient volcanic fissure eruption. Most of the columns are hexagonal, although some have four, five, seven, or eight sides. According to a legend, a form of geomyth, these columns are the remains of a causeway disappearing underwater and built by a giant.'),
			('TXT_KEY_CIV5_FEATURES_MT_EVEREST_HELP',		'The highest peak on Earth above sea level, attracting many climbers, including those with considerable experience. Although the standard route is not technically challenging, it carries hazards such as altitude sickness, weather and wind conditions, and avalanches. Hundreds of people have died leaving many bodies under the snow, unable to be recovered.'),
			('TXT_KEY_CIV5_FEATURES_RETBA_HELP',			'A salt lake overgrown with unusual pink algae, separated from the ocean only by a narrow corridor of dunes. The color is particularly visible during the dry season. The lake is known for its high salinity and is buoyant enough for people to float freely in it.'),
			('TXT_KEY_CIV5_FEATURES_BERMUDA_HELP',			'A loosely defined, mysterious area where, according to urban legend dating back to the mid-20th century, numerous planes, ships and people have mysteriously disappeared. There are many theories explaining these tragedies, ranging from paranormal phenomena to numerous natural explanations such as compass drift, the Gulf Stream, or methane hydrate, to human error and stormy weather.'),
			('TXT_KEY_CIV5_FEATURES_LUMI_BAY_HELP',			'A bay inhabited by unusual species of phytoplankton, glowing blue when stimulated. Bioluminescence is a result of many factors: water conditions and the ecosystem created by the surrounding mangrove forest, the complete absence of modern development in the lagoon, water temperature, and the depth of the bay.'),
			('TXT_KEY_CIV5_FEATURES_DALLOL_HELP',			'A cone-shaped volcano, that recorded the highest average temperature on Earth. It is known for its unusual colors and mineral patterns, as well as for the highly acidic fluids flowing from its hydrothermal springs. Because of the coexistence of such extreme physicochemical properties it is the most inhabitable place on our planet.'),
			('TXT_KEY_CIV5_FEATURES_MT_PAEKTU_HELP',		'A sacred mountain to both Korean nations, it is still an active volcano that erupts approximately every 100 years. The eruption that created the Lake of Heaven, the source of three rivers: the Songhua, Tumen, and Yalu, was one of the largest and most powerful eruptions on Earth in the last few thousands years.'),
			('TXT_KEY_CIV5_FEATURES_EYE_OF_SAHARA_HELP',	'A distinct, circular geological formation located in the heart of the desert. It is an eroded geological dome, formed by an underground magmatic intrusion that deformed the overlying sedimentary rock layers. The oldest layers are exposed at the center of the structure. It appears as concentric rings and can only be seen in its full form from the air or space.'),
			('TXT_KEY_CIV5_FEATURES_BLUE_HOLE_HELP',		'A large sinkhole close to the coast and surrounded by coral reefs and atolls. It was formed during several phases of glaciation, when sea levels were significantly lower. Due to its depth, it is a very popular diving site and a major tourist attraction. It has also been the site of several marine scientific expeditions, including the most famous one by Jacques Cousteau.'),
			('TXT_KEY_CIV5_FEATURES_GALAPAGOS_HELP',		'An isolated volcanic archipelago with unique flora and fauna. It is estimated that almost all birds, mammals and reptiles, as well as most of the plants living in this area are endemic. Biologist Charles Darwin visited the Galapagos Islands to study and catalog the plants and animals found there, and his notes and sketches became the inspiration and proof of the "theory of evolution".'),
			('TXT_KEY_CIV5_FEATURES_HA_LONG_HELP',			'A bay with thousands of limestone karsts and islets of various shapes and sizes created millions of years ago. It has been inhabited by prehistoric humanity and numerous cultures. There is a legend about the "descending dragons" that came to the bay to protect the people and to defend their country.'),
			('TXT_KEY_CIV5_FEATURES_ZHANGJIAJIE_HELP',		'Pillar-like formations being the result of years of physical erosion, not chemical erosion, which is unusual for karst areas. Its beauty inspired the unique setting of the planet Pandora in the science fiction movie "Avatar". It is also known of Bailong Elevator, literally "Elevator of a Hundred Dragons", which became the world''s highest outdoor elevator.'),
			('TXT_KEY_CIV5_FEATURES_AURORA_HELP',			'Beautiful light effects in the sky, created by the Earth''s magnetosphere as a result of the solar wind from coronal holes and coronal mass ejections. They can be observed at high latitudes, primarily at the poles, but occasionally also at lower latitudes, and can form various shapes, such as surfaces, arcs, or coronas, in a variety of colors, from red and green to blue and ultraviolet.'),
			('TXT_KEY_CIV5_FEATURES_ARCH_HELP',				'A delicate sandstone formation exposed by erosion. The arch is the most recognizable landmark and is depicted on state license plates and postage stamps. Winter Olympic Torch Relay passed through the arch, and it also presented a challenge for mountain climbers, but due to its gradual deterioration, climbing is currently prohibited.'),
			('TXT_KEY_CIV5_FEATURES_DANXIA_HELP',			'Beautiful, multicolored hills and mountains, formed million years ago from sandstone and other minerals, resembling a multi-layered cake. Thanks to wind, rain, and time carving out extraordinary shapes, including towers, pillars, and gorges of diverse colors, patterns, and sizes, it became a great target for scientists and photographers from all over the world.'),
			('TXT_KEY_CIV5_FEATURES_JEJU_DO_HELP',			'A massive volcanic caldera composed of tuff, the remains of emerging magma. It was initially separated from the island, eventually merged with it, and is now one of South Korea''s top tourist attractions. It is said that the most beautiful sunrises can be captured from its surroundings or its peak, which is why it helds the Seongsan Sunrise Festival.'),
			('TXT_KEY_CIV5_FEATURES_MARIANA_HELP',			'The deepest ocean trench on Earth over 2 km further from sea level than the summit of Mount Everest, formed by the subduction of tectonic plates. It is a common target of many research mission, mostly because of the valuable oceanic crust, oldest on Earth, or organisms living on record depths, but also because of very high pressure allowing for various tests.');